Vanta: make cookie banner handling reject-only friendly and cheaper per page.

  - CookieBannerChild: drop the MutationObserver (attributes + subtree on the
    whole body) and poll instead, each check in an idle slot, plus one
    check right after "load", since banners are often built in onload.
  - CookieBannerChild: test all presence selectors with one querySelector, so
    a page without a banner costs one DOM lookup per check.
  - CookieBannerParent: don't send rules that have nothing to click in the
    current mode (opt-in-only rules while we only reject).
  - CookieBannerListService: also import Vanta's own rules from
    vanta-site-rules.json (generated) and vanta-rules.json (hand-written)
    under chrome://global/content/cookiebanners/, after Mozilla's, so they
    can add rules and override stale ones. scripts/apply-vanta.sh copies
    both from cookiebanners/ into place. Mozilla's own tests for this
    component turn them off (cookiebanners.listService.vantaRules=false),
    since they count exact rules.
  - CookieBannerDomainPrefService: use components::AsyncShutdown::Service();
    services::GetAsyncShutdownService() no longer exists in Firefox 157+.

Applies on top of cookiebanners-1.

